infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two fixes for "Nest can't resolve dependencies"
  desc The error disappears either way — but one spawns a second instance, the other keeps one shared singleton
  compares
    - label Re-list the provider in the consumer's providers
      children
        - label Error disappears, looks fixed
          desc Compiles and resolves — the tempting one-line patch
        - label Second, separate instance
          desc A new UsersService is built inside the consuming module
        - label Shared state silently breaks
          desc Caches, in-memory data, and connections quietly diverge
    - label Export from the owner + import the owner
      children
        - label One shared singleton
          desc The same instance is injected everywhere it is needed
        - label Shared state stays consistent
          desc Caches and in-memory data live in a single object
        - label Public surface is explicit
          desc The exports array becomes a deliberate, reviewable contract
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
